 - **Pitfall:** The retrieved field may show poor overlap with target modes due to: 1) imperfect centering on the pixel grid, 2) small geometric rotation in experimental images, 3) global phase tilt and defocus, and 4) slight differences in mode waist compared to simulation [S3, unofficial].
 
 ### Back Propagation
-- **Steps:** The apodized aperture is zero-padded to the size of the full hologram to represent the hologram from that specific viewing position. It is then back-propagated using BL-ASM to reconstruct the hologram for the corresponding view. To visualize the reconstructed object, the magnitude (square root of the intensity) of the complex wavefield computed by the back propagation is extracted. This magnitude matches the gamma curves for displays and is stored as a 2D image [S4].
